Presented PHP script is prone to SSI (Server-Side Includes) injection attacks which combined
with path traversal (also called dot dot slash) attack leaks password file. The SSI attack allows to exploit website by injecting
scripts in HTML pages or attaching files with code to execute remotely. Firsth thing i did i typed "!"
as a name to see if it will be sanetized, aaaaand it wasnt. It is generaly very bad (or good, depends...)
sign when you are allowed to use characters like: < ! # = / . " - >

Than 2nd hint was .shtml web extension, that indicates (as well as .stm, .shtm) that SSI is enabled.
It was smooth sail from there on. I used command: <!--#exec cmd="ls ../" -->

It gave me list of files in main folder of the puzzle where i found file with password.